WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
In English, the past is quick.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.590
'I played.' One verb, one word.

3
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.080
French won't do that.

4
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.170
To say 'I played', it needs two words.

5
00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.120
And there's a trap for your ears.

6
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.460
Listen: «jouer», «joué».

7
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.110
The same sound, but a different spelling.

8
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:20.630
Only one of those spellings
belongs in 'I played'.

9
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.370
So what are the two words,

10
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.210
and which spelling fits?

11
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.200
In this mission, you'll
fit together a two-part key

12
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.510
and find out what each part does.

13
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.600
Then you'll build the past in the lab,

14
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.570
verb by verb, and test your predictions.

15
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.990
Your mission: crack how
French builds 'I played',

16
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.520
then build the past for any regular verb.
